For the SMC ITV2050-RC2L (RS-232C version), the communication interface is fairly simple: ASCII commands over RS-232. The official communication settings are: 9600 bps, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit (8N1), no flow control, with commands terminated by CR + LF. 

RS-232 Connector Pinout

The RS-232 communication connector uses these signals: 

Pin	Signal

2	TXD (from ITV)
3	RXD (to ITV)
4	GND
1,5	Not connected


Typical PC Wiring

PC DB9	ITV2050-RC2L

Pin 2 (RXD)	TXD
Pin 3 (TXD)	RXD
Pin 5 (GND)	GND


A USB-RS232 converter can be used if your PC lacks a COM port.

Communication Parameters

Parameter	Value

Baud Rate	9600
Data Bits	8
Parity	None
Stop Bits	1
Flow Control	None
Command Terminator	CR + LF
Character Set	ASCII


Pressure Setting Command

The RS-232 ITV series uses ASCII commands to write a pressure setpoint and read back pressure. The exact command syntax varies slightly by firmware revision, and SMC publishes it in the RS-232C Operation Manual (ITV2-OM00082 / RS-232C-E). 

Typical operation:

1. Send a pressure setpoint value.


2. ITV adjusts output pressure.


3. Read actual pressure value.


4. Monitor status/error codes.



