The ITV2050-RC2L is a pressure regulator, not a flow controller. Over RS-232 you can only command the pressure setpoint. Flow is controlled indirectly by changing the pressure. 

Main RS-232 Commands

Command	Function

SET nnn	Set pressure demand (0–1023)
REQ	Read current setpoint
MON	Read actual pressure
INC	Increase setpoint by 2 counts
DEC	Decrease setpoint by 2 counts


Example: To set 50% of full-scale pressure:

SET 512<CR><LF>

For your ITV2050 (0–0.9 MPa range), 512 corresponds to approximately:

0.9 × 512 / 1023 ≈ 0.45 MPa



Reading Back Pressure

MON<CR><LF>

Example response:

487

Actual pressure:

Pressure = 487 / 1023 × 0.9 MPa
         ≈ 0.428 MPa



If You Need Constant Flow

The ITV cannot accept commands such as:

FLOW 100
SETFLOW 50 LPM

Those commands do not exist. The device only regulates pressure. 

For closed-loop flow control you would typically use:

Flow Meter → PLC/PC → ITV2050

The PLC reads actual flow and continuously adjusts the ITV pressure using SET nnn until the desired flow is reached.

For example, if you are controlling vacuum suction through a 125 mm hose (similar to your earlier vacuum project), the logic would be:

1. Read airflow from flow sensor.


2. Compare with target flow (e.g., 500 m³/h).


3. Increase/decrease ITV pressure via SET nnn.


4. Repeat every 100–500 ms.



